learn=[('Tour the built-in families', 'Files: Read, Edit and Write. Search: Glob and Grep. Execution: Bash. Web: WebFetch and WebSearch. The live app focuses on local files, search and a fixed classroom test command.'), ('Separate availability from approval', 'tools chooses built-ins in context. allowedTools pre-approves matching calls; it does not remove unlisted tools. A bare disallowedTools name removes a tool, while a scoped deny rule leaves it visible.'), ('Observe searches and a real repair', 'Compare Glob, Grep and Read with an Edit, a Write and npm test. Independent host tests verify failure before the repair and success afterward. Original lesson fixtures remain unchanged.'), ('Compare scoped rules and callbacks', 'Bash(npm test) pre-approves that command. An unlisted extra script reaches the denying callback. Bash(npm run extra) is a scoped deny; compare attempted calls, completed tools and side effects.'), ('Protect a fake environment file', 'Read(./.env) applies to a dummy file in the private project. The real app .env is outside that project. Record whether the model attempts the Read or refuses in advance; do not invent an attempted denial.'), ('Inspect MCP-only availability', 'With tools: [], built-ins are absent while the configured classroom MCP tool remains. One actual in-process call proves this distinction. Orchestration tools and web tools are reference topics for later lessons.')]
body='<div class="flow"><div><b>01 · Select</b><p>Which tools exist in context?</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>02 · Permit</b><p>Which calls may execute?</p></div><span>→</span><div><b>03 · Verify</b><p>Actual calls and file effects</p></div></div><section class="panel" id="controls"><h2>Explore built-in tools and permissions</h2><p id="configuration" class="meta">Checking local server…</p><label for="mode">Tool experiment</label><select id="mode"><option value="read-search">Read-only · Glob → Grep → Read</option><option value="repair">Repair · Read → Edit → Write → npm test</option><option value="allow-rule">Pre-approval · npm test allowed, extra script denied</option><option value="bare-deny">Bare deny · Bash removed from context</option><option value="scoped-deny">Scoped deny · Bash visible, extra command blocked</option><option value="protect-file">Protect the private fake .env file</option><option value="mcp-only">MCP only · tools: []</option></select><button id="run" class="primary" disabled>Run tool experiment →</button><p class="meta">The host prepares a new classroom copy for every run. Commands, paths and prompts are fixed. The model cannot choose arbitrary workspaces or shell commands through this interface.</p></section><div class="workspace"><section class="panel" id="outcome"><h2 id="status" aria-live="polite">Ready</h2><p>SDK reported cost: <strong id="cost">—</strong></p><p class="meta">Session: <span id="session">—</span></p><div id="answer" class="markdown-body"></div><p id="notice" class="note"></p></section><section class="panel" id="option-panel"><h2>Options actually passed</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="options" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>Compare tools, allowedTools and disallowedTools. The separate host guard confines operations to classroom files and exact command strings. Broad Edit/Write pre-approval in Repair is scoped by that guard.</p></section></div><section class="step" id="discovery-panel"><h2>Actual tool availability</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="discovery" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>system/init.tools is the actual runtime inventory. Availability does not establish permission to execute a particular call. Tool defaults vary by platform and runtime version.</p></section><section class="step" id="evidence-panel"><h2>Actual calls, permissions and independent checks</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="evidence" class="language-json">{}</code></pre><p>PreToolUse records attempts and the separate host boundary decision. PostToolUse records completed calls; PostToolUseFailure preserves actual tool errors separately. canUseTool records unresolved permission requests and denies them. Host test exit codes and file comparisons are independent of the model’s report. protectedReadAttempted distinguishes a real Read attempt from an advance refusal.</p></section><section class="step" id="fixtures-panel"><h2>Inspect the classroom files before and after</h2><label for="fixture">Actual file snapshot</label><select id="fixture"></select><pre id="fixture-content" role="region" aria-label="Actual classroom file contents">Run an experiment to inspect the files.</pre><p>The viewer shows actual saved snapshots of the private copy. The protected dummy .env and the app’s real .env are not included here. Repair notes are shown only if the model actually created them.</p></section><section class="step" id="init-panel"><h2>Actual system/init projection</h2><pre class="json-view"><code id="init" class="language-json">{}</code></pre></section><section class="step" id="run-history"><h2>Compare this browser’s experiments</h2><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Available tools</th><th>Completed tools</th><th>Callback requests</th><th>Host test exits</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history"></tbody></table></div><button id="download">Download actual observations</button></section><section class="step" id="event-panel"><h2>Actual SDK messages and tools</h2><ul id="events"></ul></section>'
document('/','Built-in <em>tools tour.</em>','Select tools, distinguish permission from availability, then verify actual file and command effects.',body,'<script type="module" src="/client.js"></script>')
document('/learn.html','What you <em>will learn.</em>','Connect tools, rules and callbacks to observable classroom behavior.',cards(learn)+actions(('/run.html','Configure and run →'),('/architecture.html','Explore the UML →')))
env=(APP/'.env.example').read_text(encoding='utf-8').strip()
runsteps=[('Prepare the project', 'Use Node.js 24+, npm, your API key and model access. Windows needs Git Bash if the SDK cannot locate it. npm test runs only in a fresh private classroom copy.', 'cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson21-built-in-tools'), ('Install and configure', 'Preserve an existing .env, otherwise copy the safe example. Enter your key locally; the startup script explicitly loads this file.', 'npm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) {\n  Copy-Item .env.example .env\n}\nnotepad .env'), ('Start the application', 'Open port 3121 and keep the terminal running. The five linked pages cover the lab, learning goals, setup, architecture and implementation.', 'npm start\n# http://127.0.0.1:3121'), ('Search, read and repair', 'Run Read-only, then Repair. Inspect the actual call trace and before/after files. Host test exit 1 before repair and 0 afterward verify the change; tests and scripts must remain unchanged.', 'npm run sample:env -- read-search\nnpm run sample:env -- repair'), ('Compare rule layers', 'Run Allow rule, Bare deny and Scoped deny. Compare availability, attempts, completed calls and callback requests. The harmless extra script must not execute.', 'npm run sample:env -- allow-rule\nnpm run sample:env -- bare-deny\nnpm run sample:env -- scoped-deny'), ('Protect dummy data and inspect MCP-only mode', 'Run Protect file and inspect whether a Read was attempted; an advance refusal is recorded separately. Then run MCP only to call one constant tool with no built-ins in context.', 'npm run sample:env -- protect-file\nnpm run sample:env -- mcp-only\nnpm test')]
body=''
for i,(title,explanation,code) in enumerate(runsteps,1):body+=f'<section class="step" id="run-step-{i}"><span class="number">{i:02}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{explanation}</p>'+snippet(code,'powershell')+'</section>'
body+='<section class="step"><h2>Your .env configuration</h2>'+snippet(env,'dotenv')+'<p>The real key remains on the server. Restart after edits; existing shell values take precedence. No Managed Agents resource ID is needed.</p></section><section class="note"><h3>Troubleshooting</h3><p>Use the URL printed by startup. If another process occupies the port, change PORT. On Windows configure CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH if needed. Keep optional npm dependencies enabled. Inspect actual tools in initialization and distinguish native permission rules from the host guard. A failed query is never replaced by a saved answer.</p></section>'
document('/run.html','Configure and <em>run the app.</em>','Install, set your key and compare actual SDK tool experiments.',body)
specs=[('Validate the classroom experiment', 'src/agent.ts', 'if(!value ||', 'Accept a listed experiment. Browser input cannot provide arbitrary paths, shell commands or tool definitions.', 0, 1), ('Prepare a fresh fixture copy', 'src/agent.ts', 'for(const name of ["utils.js"', 'Copy trusted fixtures into a new owned working directory. The protected .env contains only a generated fake classroom token, never the app API key.', 1, 4), ('Choose built-in availability', 'src/agent.ts', 'if(mode==="read-search")', 'Select Read/Glob/Grep for inspection or Read/Edit/Write/Bash for repair. The tools array controls built-ins in the model context.', 1, 2), ('Compare pre-approval and deny rules', 'src/agent.ts', 'if(mode==="allow-rule")', 'Pre-approve npm test without removing Bash. Compare a bare Bash deny with a command-scoped deny; these operate at different layers.', 1, 3), ('Enforce the separate host boundary', 'src/agent.ts', 'const value=input.tool_input', 'The pre-tool hook records the actual target and checks fixed classroom paths and command strings. This guard is independent of native SDK permission rules.', 2, 3), ('Deny unresolved permission requests', 'src/agent.ts', 'permissionRequests.push', 'The callback records calls not already resolved by the SDK’s permission flow. In this lab it denies them; allowedTools is pre-approval, not a complete allowlist.', 3, 1), ('Run the SDK with streaming input', 'src/agent.ts', 'const run=query({prompt:input(),options});', 'An async input generator keeps the query open for the in-process MCP preview. The SDK owns the model/tool loop; the host consumes its real messages.', 1, 2), ('Inspect actual init.tools', 'src/agent.ts', 'availableTools=message.tools', 'Read the actual runtime inventory rather than assuming the requested options are the complete context. Bare deny and MCP-only experiments compare this field.', 2, 1), ('Record successful tool completion', 'src/agent.ts', 'if(input.hook_event_name==="PostToolUse")', 'PostToolUse records completed calls separately from attempts, callback requests and model claims. A blocked call must not be counted as completed.', 2, 4), ('Register the MCP-only preview', 'src/agent.ts', 'tool("course_card"', 'With tools empty, the configured MCP tool remains. Its actual handler increments a counter and returns a fixed course card; no external service is called.', 1, 2), ('Verify tests independently', 'src/agent.ts', 'try {await execute(process.execPath', 'The host invokes Node’s test runner directly in the owned copy before and after the query. This check does not rely on the model saying npm test passed.', 1, 4), ('Preserve evidence and snapshots', 'src/agent.ts', 'const testsAndScriptsUnchanged=', 'Compare test/script hashes and display actual after files. Keep original fixture integrity, dummy-data protection and model effects separate.', 1, 4), ('Format the actual answer', 'src/client.ts', 'if (e.type === "answer") renderMarkdown', 'Parse and sanitize assistant Markdown. Show typed results alongside actual call traces, permission events and independent checks.', 1, 0)]
steps=[];arrows=[];lanes=['Student UI','Node host','SDK + Claude','Permission gate','Private project']
for n,(title,source,anchor,explanation,a,b) in enumerate(specs,1):
 text=(APP/source).read_text(encoding='utf-8');lines=text.splitlines();idx=next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if anchor in l)
 count={1:2,2:3,3:2,4:3,5:3,6:3,7:2,8:2,9:2,10:3,11:3,12:3,13:3}.get(n,1);code='\n'.join(lines[idx:idx+count]).strip()
 steps.append(dict(number=n,title=title,source=source,code=code,language='typescript',explanation=explanation,firstLine=idx+1,lastLine=idx+count,anchors=[lines[idx].strip()],sourceSHA256=hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest(),narration=f'Step {n}. {explanation} This source excerpt shows the corresponding application statement.'))
 arrows.append([a,b,f'{n}. {title}'])
(APP/'scripts/architecture-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(lanes=lanes,arrows=arrows,steps=steps),indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
xs=[170,520,870,1220,1570];svg=['<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1740" height="1600" viewBox="0 0 1740 1600"><defs><marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#087fff"/></marker></defs><rect width="1740" height="1600" fill="#f4f9ff"/><text x="40" y="52" font-family="Arial" font-size="34" fill="#101a44">Lesson 21 · Select tools → permit calls → verify effects</text>']
for x,label,colour in zip(xs,lanes,['#087fff','#8838ff','#00a977','#8838ff','#ee5425']):svg.append(f'<rect x="{x-150}" y="90" width="300" height="80" rx="16" fill="{colour}"/><text x="{x}" y="139" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial" font-size="27" fill="white">{escape(label)}</text><path d="M{x} 170 V1550" stroke="#aec6df" stroke-dasharray="8 7"/>')
for i,(a,b,label) in enumerate(arrows):
 x1,x2=xs[a],xs[b];y=245+i*98;svg.append(f'<text x="{min(x1,x2)+10}" y="{y-18}" fill="#142d53" font-family="Arial" font-size="24">{escape(label)}</text><path d="M{x1} {y} H{x2}" stroke="#087fff" stroke-width="3" marker-end="url(#arrow)"/>')
(PUBLIC/'architecture.svg').write_text(''.join(svg)+'</svg>',encoding='utf-8')
walk=''
for s in steps:walk+=f'<section class="step workflow-step" id="workflow-step-{s["number"]:02}"><span class="number">{s["number"]:02}</span><h3>{s["number"]}. {s["title"]}</h3><p>{escape(s["explanation"])}</p><p class="source">Source: {s["source"]} · lines {s["firstLine"]}–{s["lastLine"]} · selected source; surrounding code omitted</p>'+snippet(s['code'])+'</section>'
document('/architecture.html','Architecture and <em>UML workflow.</em>','Every workflow step includes its corresponding coloured code excerpt.','<a class="button" href="/architecture.svg" download>Download UML SVG</a><div class="diagram"><img src="/architecture.svg" alt="Thirteen tool availability, permission and verification workflow steps"></div>'+walk)
reference=[('Core tools and permission requirements', 'Read, Glob and Grep generally run without prompts for paths inside working directories; outside paths can prompt. Bash has some read-only exceptions. Edits, writes and web operations have their own permission requirements. Platform defaults differ, so inspect initialization.'), ('Orchestration tools', 'Agent, Skill, AskUserQuestion, task tools, ToolSearch and MCP resource tools coordinate work. They are reference topics here and are not invoked in this app. WebFetch/WebSearch, notebooks and PowerShell are also reference-only.'), ('Rule format', 'ToolName(specifier) uses tool-specific command, path, domain, skill or agent matching. This app executes Bash(npm test), Bash(npm run extra) and Read(./.env) examples. Other rule examples from the slides are reference material.'), ('Cross-tool path rules', 'An Edit allow rule can grant read access. A Read deny can also affect Edit/Write on its path. This lesson’s fake-file experiment uses Read only; it does not claim to execute every cross-tool case.'), ('Independent classroom guard', 'The host limits file targets and exact commands separately from SDK pre-approval. Repair uses broad Edit/Write pre-approval while the guard permits only utils.js edits and repair-notes.md writes. Private directories are not an operating-system sandbox.'), ('Observed refusals and concurrency', 'A model may refuse a known-denied operation without calling a tool. protectedReadAttempted makes this visible. Read-only tools may run in parallel, but this app does not require or claim a particular scheduling order.'), ('MCP preview', 'The one constant in-process MCP tool completes the slide’s tools: [] exercise. The next lesson explains authoring custom tools in depth. Built-in availability is distinct from configured MCP tools.'), ('Short temporary workspaces', 'Generated projects use short paths under the operating system temporary directory. This avoids Windows shell bookkeeping failures caused by deeply nested course paths. The original fixtures and real application .env remain in the application folder.')]

document('/walkthrough.html','How the app <em>was built.</em>','Thirteen coloured source excerpts connect availability, permission flow and verified effects.',cards(reference)+walk)
readme='# Claude Agent SDK · Lesson 21 · Built-in tools tour\n\nBased on Lesson21_Built_in_Tools_Tour.pptx. Five student pages, large text and coloured code for all 13 UML steps.\n\n## What you will learn\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in learn)
readme+='\n## Configure and run\n\n```powershell\ngit clone https://github.com/luiscoco/Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson21-app.git\ncd .\\Udemy-Claude-Agent-SDK-lesson21-app\nnpm ci\nif (!(Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item .env.example .env }\nnotepad .env\nnpm start\n```\n\nFrom presentations use `cd .\\agent-sdk\\lesson21-built-in-tools` instead of cloning. Open http://127.0.0.1:3121 and keep the terminal running.\n\n## Create your .env file\n\nPreserve an existing file or copy .env.example, enter your own key locally and restart after edits. Shell values take precedence. Node.js 24+ and model access are required; Windows may need Git Bash.\n\n```dotenv\n'+env+'\n```\n\nThe real app .env is separate from the generated fake file in the exercise. Neither file is committed.\n\n## Run the experiments\n\n'
for title,explanation,code in runsteps[3:]:readme+=f'### {title}\n\n{explanation}\n\n```powershell\n{code}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## How the app was built\n\n'
for step in steps:readme+=f'### {step["number"]}. {step["title"]}\n\n{step["explanation"]}\n\nSource: `{step["source"]}`, lines {step["firstLine"]}–{step["lastLine"]}. Selected source; surrounding code omitted.\n\n```typescript\n{step["code"]}\n```\n\n'
readme+='## Reference topics and limits\n\n'+''.join(f'- {a}: {b}\n' for a,b in reference)+'\nMedia, .env, dependencies and private runtime files remain local and excluded from Git. No stored answer replaces an actual result.\n\n## References\n\n- [Tools reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference)\n- [SDK permissions](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/permissions)\n- [Custom tool preview](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/custom-tools)\n\nRegenerate student pages with `python scripts/build-pages.py`.\n'
(APP/'README.md').write_text(readme,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built five Lesson 21 pages and 13 source-matched UML steps.')
